comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T17:13:56.827Z",pi-agent,"All eleven findings resolved; every refusal added this round was verified revert-proof (guard reverted, pinned test confirmed to FAIL, restored from git).\n\n- 3836312702 (empty verdict): deriveVerdict now refuses an empty result set with typed code empty_gate_results instead of vacuously passing — an absent measurement can never render as a pass. Revert-proof: with the guard removed the pinned test FAILS.\n- 3836312741 (whitespace bypass): metric names are trimmed BEFORE the uniqueness check and the normalized value stored; \"reward\" and \" reward \" now collide (invalid_transfer_gaps). Revert-proof verified. Internal spacing differences remain distinct metrics, covered by a dedicated test.\n- 3836312710 (plan atomicity): the sweep id itself is pre-checked (sweep_exists) alongside every arm id (sweep_arm_exists), so an ownerless sweep can never be re-armed; a mid-plan failure now removes every arm the invocation wrote (removePlannedArms) and the removal-failure path is refused with BOTH causes named (sweep_cleanup_failed). Proven with injected mid-write failures: a second-create failure leaves zero orphaned runs, and a failing removal surfaces both causes.\n- 3836312711 (resolved ids): the degenerate check now compares RESOLVED environment identities after both sides verify; two spellings of one environment (alias-scoped prefix normalized away) are refused. Revert-proof verified.\n- 3836312706 (heading anchor): fencedSection anchors headings to a line start; regression test embeds the heading in caller-supplied algorithm text — under the unanchored search the test FAILS (verify reads the wrong fence), with the anchor it passes.\n- 3836312715 (caching): staleness reasons are cached per environment id in transfer gap, matching the leaderboard pattern.\n- 3836312718 (duplicates): package.json deduplicated.\n- 3836312726 (candidate rule): parseSweepSpec now enforces the non-empty candidate array its message states, with the test case.\n- 3836312730 (gpgsign): commit.gpgsign=false pinned on every commit/merge in the sweep git-merge test.\n- 3836312732 (helper type): plan helper returns Promise<unknown>.\n- 3836312746 (upstream note): the UPSTREAM-ISSUES.md entry was retracted entirely — the flagged contract was an error in the instruction file, not the CLI.\n\nMeasured gates after all fixes: npm run release:check exit 0; npm test 230/230 pass; coverage 100/100/100 across 17 source files; docstring gate 17 file(s), 124 declaration(s); jscpd 0 clones at the zero-tolerance threshold; ./.bin/pm health --strict-exit green (pinned binary). No threshold lowered, no exclusion added.\n"
  "2026-08-24T09:30:47.435Z",pi-agent,"Review follow-up (PR 16 round 3): provenance for the health claim recorded in this history stream. The pinned binary used for pm health strict-exit is ./node_modules/.bin/pm, version 2026.8.20 (devDependency @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.20). History is append-only and hash-chained, so the exact provenance is recorded as this new corrective entry rather than by rewriting the earlier record."
close_reason: "All eleven CodeRabbit findings resolved with tests; the two new refusals (empty_gate_results, sweep_cleanup_failed) and the normalization/anchor/resolved-id guards each verified revert-proof. Gates: release:check exit 0, 230/230 tests, 100/100/100 coverage across 17 files, docstring 124 declarations, jscpd 0 clones."
